## Assumptions Made

1. **Shared financial records** — All financial records belong to the organization,
   not individual users. Any authorized user can view all records.

2. **First admin via seed** — The first admin account is created automatically
   when the server starts for the first time. There is no public API to create an admin.

3. **New users default to viewer** — Anyone who registers through the public
   register API gets the viewer role. Only an admin can promote them.

4. **Soft deactivation** — Users are never deleted from the database.
   They are deactivated using the is_active flag. This preserves data integrity
   since records reference users via foreign key.

5. **Records are never truly deleted** — Deleted records are permanently removed.
   A future improvement would be soft delete with a deleted_at column.

6. **Amount is always positive** — The type field (income or expense) determines
   the direction of the money. Amount itself is always a positive number.

7. **Date is stored as text** — SQLite has no native date type. Dates are stored
   as YYYY-MM-DD strings which sort correctly alphabetically.

